@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;architecture] book-is-built-from-the-kit
The UI Book is built from the same kit and tokens as the screens, so what it shows is
what ships. It has no look of its own (DESIGN.md UI Book).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] book-one-page-list
`book.json` is the one typed list of the book's pages and components. Every page without
a component has a route in `BookRoutes.kt`, every route has a page, and every component
has exactly one default variant and its previews (book check).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] book-shows-both-themes
A component page shows every state in light and dark, side by side or one at a time, and
the Component specs page measures each sized component against DESIGN.md on the phone
(rules 44 and 47).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] book-lists-every-contract
The Contracts page lists every contract of every `CONTRACTS` file bundled at build time,
grouped by the area of the code it governs, named in plain words, with a fold per area, a
label filter (All, Product, Design, Motion, Architecture, Security) and a search over IDs
and prose. Each contract shows its ID in the code font, its labels and its prose drawn as
Markdown. Nothing on the page is typed by hand (message 15 Oct).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] book-contracts-parse-cleanly
The bundled contracts MUST parse with the app's parser with no problems: every contract
has an owner and a label, non-empty prose, and an ID used once in its file and its parent
`CONTRACTS` files. A unit test reads the bundle the APK ships and fails otherwise.
